<title>USA: Chicago Milwaukee to make distribution.</title>
<headline>Chicago Milwaukee to make distribution.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chicago Milwaukee Corp said a distribution of remaining funds under its plan of liquidation would be made on or about October 25 to shareholders of record on May 22.</p>
<p>The distribution will amount to $1.65 per share, said the directors and trustees of the company.</p>
<p>Chicago Milwaukee was the holding company for the Chicago, Milwaukee, St. Paul and Pacific Railroad Co, also called the Milwaukee Road, and several other subsidiaries. All were sold following the Milwaukee Road reogranization in 1985, the company said.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
